{"seq":18,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-min-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:01:59.864Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f9e62bcb0f0a5317d01a72d4fce0dbeb0373d48c19edeb9a62f4880024bef914","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Tobias, I found three ticket numbers that look like Marrow Fieldworks. One caveat: nothing in these sources names Marrow Fieldworks right next to a ticket number. They say \"Pree's dealer account\" or \"Tobias's dealer account\", so I've matched them by context.\n\n*From Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (teams/team-central/digests, dated 2 Jan 2026)*\nThis digest says Marrow Fieldworks changes hands on Mon 5 Jan 2026. It then lists two open tickets that Hollis flagged on \"Pree's dealer account\" before that handoff:\n• *#4409*: the Gatehouse Check-In report keeps timing out at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake).\n• *#4412*: a small glitch in the driver SMS prompt when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n\n*From #central-random (13 Oct 2026, 09:27, your own message)*\n• *#8841*: West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. That message is about \"Tobias's dealer account\". I'm assuming that's Marrow Fieldworks after the January handoff, but nothing I can see confirms it, so please check.\n\n*Similar names I left out:*\n• FR-882, in the same Moss digest, is a feature request from Marrow *Agrisupply*, which is a different account (the Central team's ag account).\n• PD-4821 in #central-team is also Marrow Agrisupply.\n• Moss's North digests have #4419 and #PD-4492, but both are Quarrendon Freight Lines.\n\nMoss's other Central file, the cheat sheet, has no ticket numbers. There's no separate notes folder for Moss, so I used the public Moss digests."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-min-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:02:05.858Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"6bc833a2c4e248a0aac9ae9996fe976125f41ee72ffd5a1296d1bdb4fb399032","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three ticket numbers that look like Marrow Fieldworks. None of my sources puts the name Marrow Fieldworks right next to a ticket number, though, so I matched them by context.\n\n**From Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" note (2 Jan 2026)**\nThe note says Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Monday 5 Jan 2026. It lists two open tickets Hollis flagged on \"Pree's dealer account\" before that handoff:\n- **#4409:** the Gatehouse Check-In report keeps timing out at the Salina North yard. It happens at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake.\n- **#4412:** a small glitch in the text-message prompt drivers get when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n\n**From #central-random (your own message, 13 Oct 2026, 09:27)**\n- **#8841:** at the Plains depots, West yard Door 2 double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. That message was about \"Tobias's dealer account\". I'm assuming that's Marrow Fieldworks since the January handoff, but nothing I can see confirms it, so please check.\n\n**Similar names I left out**\n- **FR-882** (in the same Moss note) and **PD-4821** (in #central-team) both belong to Marrow Agrisupply, which is a different account.\n- **#4419** and **#PD-4492** (in Moss's North team notes) are Quarrendon Freight Lines.\n\nMoss doesn't have a personal notes folder, so I used Moss's notes in the shared team folders. The only other Central one, a cheat sheet, has no ticket numbers.\n\nI've also posted this list in our DM."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
